# Nothing here belongs in a static deployment.
#
# server/ is deliberately excluded: it keeps state in an in-memory Map and runs
# module-scope setInterval timers, neither of which survives a serverless
# function's lifecycle. Deploying it as a Vercel function would produce an
# account that resets between requests — worse than not deploying it at all.
# With no /api routes present, api-client.js's probe() 404s and the game falls
# back to its local simulation, which is the intended static behaviour.
server/
test/
node_modules/
package-lock.json
QA-NOTES.md
cli.js
bin/
.git/
